tests: free the compute context of test-opt
Fold-into: upstream/ggml-core

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 plus every patch of the series before this one.

test_regression() of tests/test-opt.cpp creates ctx_compute with ggml_init
and does not free it: ggml_opt_fit and ggml_opt_free free only the contexts
of the optimizer, not a context of the caller. LeakSanitizer reports the
ggml_context of each of the two optimizer types and its memory. The upstream
CMake file does not build test-opt with LLAMA_SANITIZE_ADDRESS for this
reason.

The change: ggml_free(ctx_compute) at the end of test_regression. Test code
only.

diff --git a/tests/test-opt.cpp b/tests/test-opt.cpp
index 8dcb4a7..7220f46 100644
--- a/tests/test-opt.cpp
+++ b/tests/test-opt.cpp
@@ -834,6 +834,7 @@ static std::pair<int, int> test_regression(
 
     ggml_backend_buffer_free(buf);
     ggml_free(ctx_static);
+    ggml_free(ctx_compute);
     ggml_opt_dataset_free(dataset);
 
     return std::make_pair(npass, ntest);
